{"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event is a value conforming to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" is a value: tracking an event records it as an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", with its timestamp, the caller’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SourceLocation"},{"type":"text","text":" and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":", as one of the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"records"},{"type":"text","text":". Delivering is a chain of operators over that sequence: Afluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch(strategy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"type":"text","text":", the default) gathers the records into batches, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" hands each batch to every destination, as a lazy unit of work. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destination"},{"type":"text","text":" is a plain sink, narrowed or transformed by its modifiers: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepting(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"droppingCallSite()"},{"type":"text","text":". A tracker given a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Consent"},{"type":"text","text":" delivers an event only once the user grants its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ConsentCategory"},{"type":"text","text":", holding it while undecided and dropping it when denied. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"type":"text","text":" only queues an event, from any thread; a worker the tracker owns, never on the main actor, does the rest. A tracker given a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" writes each record to disk as its worker reaches it and delivers what an earlier run left first. A property whose valid values are narrower than its type is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"type":"text","text":" value, which satisfies its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refinement"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Constraint"},{"type":"text","text":"s from the moment it is made, or carries constraints declared with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"type":"text","text":"; the tracker’s worker rejects an event that breaks one before anything else, reporting each as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RejectionReport"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rejectionReports"},{"type":"text","text":". On Apple platforms, SwiftUI views read the tracker from the environment and track what they do with view modifiers, and a screen’s events carry its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenKey"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). UIKit views and view controllers inherit it as a trait, the same value as SwiftUI’s, set on a window scene ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and AppKit views find it up their responder chain ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"); a control’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks an event through the tracker found when its action fires, so each scene or window can have its own. Screen views can track themselves once a window scene or window turns it on with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreensAutomatically"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenViewed"},{"type":"text","text":" as each screen’s view controller appears, without swizzling ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and UIKit controls once a window scene turns it on with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackControlsAutomatically"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ControlActivated"},{"type":"text","text":" as a touch activates each control named by its accessibility identifier ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). On every platform, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackLifecycle"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and makes the tracker’s records durable as it leaves the foreground ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions"},{"type":"text","text":" enricher stamps every event with its session’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", a random identifier held in memory only, and starts a new session after a timeout of inactivity, tracking "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionEnded"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler"},{"type":"text","text":"s keeps a seeded fraction of the events they apply to, event by event, or whole sessions with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)"},{"type":"text","text":", dropping the rest on its worker before they are held, written or delivered, reporting each drop as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SamplingDropReport"},{"type":"text","text":" and stamping each kept record with its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SampleRateKey"},{"type":"text","text":". The standard enrichers, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.application()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operatingSystem()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vendorIdentifier()"},{"type":"text","text":", stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale, network connection and the platform’s identifier for vendor, each under a typed key, the static ones read once ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" imports every module but ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","isActive":true},{"text":", a product of its own for apps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that already use GRDB; ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","isActive":true},{"text":", whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" macro derives an event’s conformances","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and schema from its declaration and which alone builds swift-syntax; ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","isActive":true},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exports those schemas as a JSON Schema tracking plan and checks the events against a committed one;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","isActive":true},{"text":", which runs that check from an app’s tests; and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","isActive":true},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"text":" gives a test’s body a fresh tracker and returns what it tracked. Each module also has its own documentation and can be imported on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Traffluent","","struct SignedUp: Event {","    var plan: String","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"Traffluent","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Traffluent","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"],"anchor":"Modules","title":"Modules"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting"],"anchor":"Testing","title":"Testing"}],"references":{"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/destinations","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","kind":"symbol","title":"Destinations","role":"collection"},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","kind":"symbol","title":"AppKitTracking","role":"collection"},"doc://LifecycleTracking/documentation/LifecycleTracking":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/lifecycletracking","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","kind":"symbol","title":"LifecycleTracking","role":"collection"},"doc://TrackerTesting/documentation/TrackerTesting":{"role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"TrackerTesting","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trackertesting","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WhatGoesWhere":{"role":"article","title":"Logging, Tracing, Metrics and Analytics","abstract":[{"text":"Four signals, four jobs. Decide which one a fact belongs to before you write the line that records it.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/whatgoeswhere"},"doc://UIKitTracking/documentation/UIKitTracking":{"role":"collection","title":"UIKitTracking","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/uikittracking"},"doc://AutomaticControlTracking/documentation/AutomaticControlTracking":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/automaticcontroltracking","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","kind":"symbol","title":"AutomaticControlTracking","role":"collection"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"role":"collection","title":"HTTPDestinations","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations"},"doc://Checksums/documentation/Checksums":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/checksums","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums","kind":"symbol","title":"Checksums","role":"collection"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"role":"collection","title":"TrackingPlanTesting","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/IdentifyingPeople":{"abstract":[{"text":"Traffluent knows people only by a pseudonymous session. An identifier that outlives one is yours to add, store, reset and gate with consent.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/identifyingpeople","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","kind":"article","title":"Identifying People","role":"article"},"doc://AutomaticScreenTracking/documentation/AutomaticScreenTracking":{"role":"collection","title":"AutomaticScreenTracking","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking"},"doc://LoggingDestinations/documentation/LoggingDestinations":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/loggingdestinations","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","kind":"symbol","title":"LoggingDestinations","role":"collection"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"role":"collection","title":"TracingDestinations","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","kind":"symbol","title":"TrackingPlans","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PrivacyManifests":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","kind":"article","title":"Privacy Manifests","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Traffluent"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events":{"role":"collection","title":"Events","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/events"},"doc://StandardContext/documentation/StandardContext":{"role":"collection","title":"StandardContext","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/standardcontext"},"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"role":"collection","title":"GRDBPersistence","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}],"title":"Changing an Event","kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking":{"role":"collection","title":"SwiftUITracking","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"role":"collection","title":"Persistence","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/trackers","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","kind":"symbol","title":"Trackers","role":"collection"},"doc://Sessions/documentation/Sessions":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/sessions","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","kind":"symbol","title":"Sessions","role":"collection"},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","kind":"symbol","title":"EventMacros","role":"collection"}}}